# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Secrets
.env

# Hermes workspace-local plans (plan skill output). Plans are preserved in the
# Obsidian vault (Portfolio-GitHub/History/), not in the public repo.
.hermes/

# Persistence store — runtime state, not source. Historically a sqlite db;
# now the harness FileStepStore writes a directory of JSON/JSONL under
# data/paf/. Ignore the runtime tree. `data/*` (not `data/`) keeps the root
# traversable so the `!` exceptions can re-include a subtree.
data/*
!.env.example
!data/benchmarks/
data/benchmarks/*
!data/benchmarks/generated/
# Journal-sandbox oracle stem: OUR derived data (copy of lme_oracle.json under
# a distinct stem so journal-format durables namespace to memory-lme_oracle_journal/).
# Tracked so a fresh clone can restore those journal durables and re-run the
# soft-verify/prompt experiments. The upstream lme_oracle.json bank stays ignored.
!data/benchmarks/lme_oracle_journal.json
# Durable seed summaries under generated/ are auto-persisted by run_lmem.py
# (_persist_durable_summary) per seeded question and TRACKED so a fresh clone
# re-runs zero-live-summarizer. They rename only when a question's seed turns
# change. Keep any non-summary churn (e.g. transient run dumps) out via
# explicit ignores below.
data/benchmarks/generated/*
!data/benchmarks/generated/*.jsonl

# Durable per-question memory snapshots are auto-persisted by run_lmem.py
# (_persist_durable_memory) per seeded question and TRACKED so a fresh clone
# re-runs with ZERO owner/consolidation tokens. Each <qid>/ holds the
# owner-produced memory store (assistant/MEMORY.md + assistant/.memory-state.json).
# The split (oracle vs _s/_m) is namespaced by the LME data-file stem:
# memory-lme_oracle/ , memory-longmemeval_s_cleaned/ , etc. The negation below
# re-includes the memory-*/ dir that `data/benchmarks/*` would ignore; once the
# dir is included git descends and tracks everything under it. Refresh via
# PAF_FRESH_MEMORY=1 (or LME_QIDS=<qid> PAF_FRESH_MEMORY=1), which re-consolidates
# and overwrites the snapshot.
!data/benchmarks/memory-*/

# Generated benchmark run outputs (graded runner writes JSON per full run).
tests/results/

# Demo scratch database (ui/cli_demo.py)
demo.db
